{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"119580","commit":"abe15c69ae0d6d47bd3989d291b6c27c903a604c","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of `ESQL_SKIP_ES_INDEX_SERIALIZATION` and related changes seem to be aimed at optimizing serialization by avoiding the serialization of `EsIndex` objects. However, there is a potential issue with backward compatibility. The code assumes that if the transport version is before `ESQL_SKIP_ES_INDEX_SERIALIZATION`, it should read a boolean value that was previously written for the `frozen` field in `EsRelation`. This boolean value is no longer written when the transport version is on or after `ESQL_SKIP_ES_INDEX_SERIALIZATION`. If an older node tries to deserialize data from a newer node, it will fail because the boolean value for `frozen` is missing. Ensure that backward compatibility is maintained by either writing a placeholder boolean value or handling the absence of this field gracefully. The changes in these diffs involve replacing `EsIndex` with `indexPattern` and adding `indexNameWithModes`. Ensure that all places where `EsIndex` was used have been updated to handle the new fields correctly. Specifically, verify that any logic relying on the `mapping()` method of `EsIndex` is now handled appropriately using `indexNameWithModes`.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/EsSourceExec.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/EsSourceExec.java--2273:3172","promptId":"#NNZ19","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/EsSourceExec.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/physical/EsSourceExec.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2273,"endPos":3172,"startLine":63,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":79,"endLineOffset":5,"length":900}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/planner/PlannerUtils.java-